          "If you used force to protect yourself or someone else, tell only your lawyer. Florida law can make lawful force a reason you cannot be prosecuted at all. That question comes up early, so it should be raised the right way.",
          "Read your release papers and follow every condition. Release comes with a rule of no contact of any kind with the victim. The only exception is the formal evidence exchange in the case. Only the court can change this rule, on a motion showing good cause and that justice requires the change.",
