          "Under organized fraud, each message sent to carry out the plan can be its own charge. A judge can give a separate sentence for each one. A maximum is a ceiling, not a forecast.",
          "Florida also adds up points to set the lowest sentence. For most third degree felonies that are not forcible felonies (violent crimes named in the law, plus any other felony that uses or threatens force against a person), 22 points or less means the judge must give a sentence outside state prison. Burglary-type felonies are left out of that rule. The judge can impose prison only with written findings that a non-prison sentence could put the public in danger.",
