          "The two laws do not cover the same ground. Florida's law reaches any investment or security, and investment advice too. That includes securities and sales that are exempt from registration.",
          "The federal law is tied to the type of asset. It covers any security (stock, bond, note and so on) of a company that has a class of securities registered under the Securities Exchange Act of 1934, or that is required to file reports under it. It also covers a commodity for future delivery and an option on one. So a deal can fit Florida's law and still fall outside the federal one.",
